{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Day With Vanessa"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Art Exhibit"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><br/>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The man <span class=\"strong\">who/that</span> called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">man</span> - the noun it describes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book <span class=\"strong\">which/that</span> I lent you was my father's.</span><br/>Which book? The book I lent you."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative connector</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of Relative Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Ai Wei Wei is an artist who is also considered to be an activist. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who is considered to be an activist\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">This is the sign which represents me, no?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which represents me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There are certain attributes that people associate with each sign.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" that people associate with each sign\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About the Future - If, When, Before and After"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use time clauses to give information about time and sequence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words If, When, Before and After in time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional with these time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If/When/Before/After + Subject + Simple Present tense, Subject + will/be going to + Simple Present tense"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Before</span> means at an earlier time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">After</span> means at a later time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Before I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm.<br/>After I set my alarm, I'm going to go to sleep.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> means on the condition that ... "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm. (I'm not sure that I'll go to sleep).</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> means at the time of doing something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When I go to bed, I'll set my alarm.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'll do some research about it when I get home."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before you do that, let's try to guess! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they have a miniature horse sculpture in the gift shop, I'm going to buy it! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "After this, are we going to go for lunch? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bronze"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a yellowish-brown metal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The sculptures are made of bronze."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about art."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "zodiac"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a repeating cycle of 12 years, with each year being represented by an animal and its attributes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a bronze sculpture for each animal of the zodiac. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dynasty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a line of rulers of a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Qing dynasty of China was from 1644-1912."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feature"}, {"type": "pa